  "sourceProperties": {
    "Recommendation": "Note: updating an SSL policy may reduce compatibility for users with outdated versions of TLS. This target proxy uses the default GCP SSL policy. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/net-services/loadbalancing/advanced/targetProxies/list?project=example-project and find the row with the target proxy \"gkegw1-abcd-gateway-system-example-gateway-0000000000.\" Note the forwarding rules in the \"In use by\" column. Then, follow the instructions at https://cloud.google.com/load-balancing/docs/use-ssl-policies to either create a new or update an existing SSL policy with a \"Minimum TLS version\" of 1.2 and a Modern or Restricted \"Profile.\" If a Custom profile is desired, make sure [TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA, TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA, TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256, TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA, TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384] are all disabled. Apply the SSL policy to each forwarding rule you previously noted.",
    "ExceptionInstructions": "Add the security mark \"allow_weak_ssl_policy\" to the asset with a value of \"true\" to prevent this finding from being activated again.",
    "Explanation": "HTTPS and SSL Proxy load balancers use SSL policies to determine the protocol and cipher suites used in the TLS connections established between users and the Internet. These connections encrypt sensitive data to prevent malicious eavesdroppers from accessing it. A weak SSL policy permits clients using outdated versions of TLS to connect with a less secure cipher suite or protocol. For a list of recommended and outdated cipher suites, see https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-parameters/tls-parameters.xhtml#tls-parameters-4.",
    "ScannerName": "COMPUTE_INSTANCE_SCANNER",
    "ResourcePath": [
      "projects/example-project/",
      "folders/111111111111/",
      "folders/222222222222/",
      "organizations/123456789012/"
